What is ReactJS?
 ReactJS is a JavaScript library used to build user interfaces (UI), mainly for web 
apps.
 It is component-based, meaning the UI is broken into reusable parts (components).
 Created by Facebook, it makes building dynamic, interactive web pages easier and 
faster.
Why use ReactJS?
1. Reusable Components – Write a component once, use it anywhere.
2. Fast Rendering – Uses Virtual DOM (DOM stands for Document Object Model.) 
to update only the changed parts of the page.
3. Easy to Write UI – JSX(JSX stands for JavaScript XML write HTML-like code 
inside JavaScript.) lets you write HTML-like code in JavaScript.
4. Component Nesting – Build complex UIs by combining small components.
5. Popular in Industry – Many modern web apps (Facebook, Instagram) use React.
