5(a) Render HTML
 What it means: Display simple HTML content on a web page using React.
 Example: Show a heading or paragraph.
 Why use: Helps beginners understand how React renders content.
Rendering means showing content on the screen.
In normal HTML, the browser shows <h1>Hello</h1> directly.
In React, we write HTML inside a component (like a function). 
React then renders (displays) that HTML into the browser.
We use root.render(<App />) to tell React what to show.
Example:
fnction App() {
return <h1>Hello Students</h1>;
}
This will render (show) “Hello Students” on the web page. 
Without render, our code just sits in VS Code – users cannot see it.
 React re-renders automatically if data changes (fast updates).
Open App.js
 In VS Code sidebar → open src/App.js.
Program5(a):
import Reactfrom"react"; 
function App() 
{ return <h1>Hello, React!</h1>;// Renders plain HTML
 }
export default App;
